course: dictionary
lesson: 8292
title: Risky: what could go wrong?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Risky means possibly dangerous: something that could make you get hurt, lose something or go wrong. «Going down stairs is riskier than going up, because a slip sends you forward and down.» Riskier means more risky, so going down is the more dangerous of the two.
explain: When you meet a risky thing, ask three questions: What could go wrong? How likely is it? How bad would it be? A small risk can be fine with safety gear, like a helmet, but a big risk is not worth it.
explain: Risky does not mean you will definitely get hurt. It means harm is possible. «Many childhood injuries happen when children are bored and try risky things to pass the time.» The word warns you about the chance of harm.
fact: Risky means possibly dangerous; it could make you get hurt, lose something or go wrong.
fact: Riskier means more risky, and riskiest means the most risky.
fact: Useful phrases: «too risky», «a risky plan», «it's risky to».
fact: In stories, a risky plan builds suspense, because the reader wonders what will happen.
fact: Good safety questions are: What could go wrong? How likely? How bad?
exercise: What does risky mean? | *Possibly dangerous | Sleepy and slow | Full of water | Very colourful
exercise: «Going down stairs is riskier than going up.» Which is more dangerous? | *Going down | Going up | They are exactly the same | Neither one is ever a risk
exercise: Which of these is a risky thing to do? | *Cross a busy road without looking | Eat your lunch | Read a book | Drink a glass of water
test: Which phrase means it could be dangerous to do something? | *It's risky to climb onto the roof | Very tasty | Full of colour | Nice and warm
test: What is the best question to ask about a risky thing? | Who made it? | How old is it? | What colour is it? | *What could go wrong?
exam: Which word means the most risky? | Riskier | *Riskiest | Riskily | Risky
